/ Smart Match capability fields.
/
/ Every yes/no control here is TRI-STATE, not a checkbox, and that is
/ deliberate. The columns are nullable and SmartMatch::RuleScorer treats NULL
/ as "nobody has told us" -- skipping the rule entirely rather than scoring it
/ as a "no". A plain checkbox can only say true/false, so an untouched form
/ would record a definite "we do not offer this" for every organization that
/ never opened the page. See docs/smart-match-scoring/06-phase-5-fields.md.
/
/ "Not specified" submits an empty string, which ActiveRecord casts back to
/ NULL for a boolean column. The radio trio lives in _smart_match_tristate.
/
/ Questions are grouped by which visitor the answer matches the organization
/ to, in the order the quiz asks: find help, volunteer, donate. That mirrors
/ config/smart_match_scoring.yml, where every field below is scored on exactly
/ one quiz path, so a nonprofit filling in only the audiences it cares about
/ can stop at the end of a group.

section class="mt-6 text-gray-2" id="smart-match-fields"
  h4 class="text-lg font-medium leading-7 text-gray-2" Smart Match Details
  p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-4"
    | These answers help Smart Match recommend your organization to the right people.
    |  Every question is optional — leaving one as
    strong  "Not specified"
    |  simply means we won't use it when matching, and will never count against you.

  h5 class="mt-6 text-sm font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-gray-4"
    | For people looking for services
  .grid.grid-cols-12.gap-4
    - Organizations::Constants::SMART_MATCH_SERVICE_QUESTIONS.each do |attribute, question|
      = render "organizations/smart_match_tristate", f: f, attribute: attribute, question: question

    / Languages -- a blank set stays NULL ("not answered"), so the hidden field
    / that normally submits an empty array is deliberately omitted.
    fieldset class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7 md:col-span-6 mt-6"
      legend class="text-sm font-medium leading-4 text-gray-2"
        | Which languages can you deliver services in?
      div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6 mt-3"
        - Organizations::Constants::LANGUAGES.each do |language|
          div class="flex items-center gap-2"
            = check_box_tag "organization[languages][]", language, Array(f.object.languages).include?(language), id: "organization_languages_#{language.parameterize.underscore}", class: "h-4 w-4 rounded-6px text-blue-medium focus:ring-0 focus:ring-transparent"
            = label_tag "organization_languages_#{language.parameterize.underscore}", language, class: "text-sm text-black"

    / Leadership sits with the service questions because that is where it is
    / scored: the service seeker's preferences step, not a giving question.
    fieldset class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7 md:col-span-6 mt-6"
      legend class="text-sm font-medium leading-4 text-gray-2"
        | Is your organization women-led or BIPOC-led?
      div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6 mt-3"
        - Organizations::Constants::LEADERSHIP_ATTRIBUTES.each do |attribute|
          div class="flex items-center gap-2"
            = check_box_tag "organization[leadership_attributes][]", attribute, Array(f.object.leadership_attributes).include?(attribute), id: "organization_leadership_#{attribute.parameterize.underscore}", class: "h-4 w-4 rounded-6px text-blue-medium focus:ring-0 focus:ring-transparent"
            = label_tag "organization_leadership_#{attribute.parameterize.underscore}", attribute, class: "text-sm text-black"

  h5 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-gray-4"
    | For volunteers
  .grid.grid-cols-12.gap-4
    div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7 md:col-span-6 mt-2"
      = f.label :volunteer_format, "What format do your volunteer opportunities take?", class: "block text-sm text-gray-3 font-medium"
      = f.select :volunteer_format, Organizations::Constants::VOLUNTEER_FORMATS, { include_blank: "Not specified" }, { class: "block h-46px mt-1 w-full py-0 px-4 rounded-6px border-gray-5 text-base text-gray-3 focus:ring-blue-medium focus:border-blue-medium" }

    fieldset class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-7 md:col-span-6 mt-6"
      legend class="text-sm font-medium leading-4 text-gray-2"
        | What time commitments do your volunteer roles involve?
      div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6 mt-3"
        - Organizations::Constants::VOLUNTEER_FREQUENCIES.each do |frequency|
          div class="flex items-center gap-2"
            = check_box_tag "organization[volunteer_frequency][]", frequency, Array(f.object.volunteer_frequency).include?(frequency), id: "organization_volunteer_frequency_#{frequency.parameterize.underscore}", class: "h-4 w-4 rounded-6px text-blue-medium focus:ring-0 focus:ring-transparent"
            = label_tag "organization_volunteer_frequency_#{frequency.parameterize.underscore}", frequency, class: "text-sm text-black"

    - Organizations::Constants::SMART_MATCH_VOLUNTEER_QUESTIONS.each do |attribute, question|
      = render "organizations/smart_match_tristate", f: f, attribute: attribute, question: question

  h5 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-gray-4"
    | For donors
  .grid.grid-cols-12.gap-4
    - Organizations::Constants::SMART_MATCH_GIVING_QUESTIONS.each do |attribute, question|
      = render "organizations/smart_match_tristate", f: f, attribute: attribute, question: question
